{
  "_comment": [
    "Every Gemini UI hook lives in this file so a UI change never requires touching Python code.",
    "Each entry is an ordered list of candidate locators; the browser layer tries them in order",
    "and uses the first one that actually resolves to a visible element on the page.",
    "Locator kinds: 'role' (role + name), 'label', 'placeholder', 'testid', 'text', 'css'.",
    "'name'/'text' values are matched case-insensitively as substrings (Playwright regex),",
    "so English and Arabic UI variants can be listed side by side.",
    "Page state matters when a hook seems missing: 'send_button' normally appears only after",
    "text is typed into the composer, and every response hook (stop_button, response_container,",
    "response_complete_marker, generated_image, image_download_button, image_more_options_button)",
    "exists only while/after an answer is on screen. Run '--mode inspect --probe' to check those.",
    "If no candidate matches, the agent falls back to DOM heuristics (the button beside the",
    "composer, the large image that appeared after sending), so a rename degrades speed, not the run."
  ],
